        <div id="target-humidity" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-16 mb-6">
            4. Target Humidity by Room, Basement and Crawl Space
          </h2>

          <p>
            The EPA recommends keeping indoor humidity below 60 percent and ideally between 30 and 50 percent. That band is a compromise between two sets of problems. Below 30 percent, skin, sinuses and wood floors dry out and static builds. Above 50 percent, dust mites thrive, and once humidity stays above 60 percent for long stretches, mold and mildew get a foothold on cool surfaces.
          </p>

          <div class="overflow-hidden border border-gray-200 rounded-2xl my-8">
            <div class="overflow-x-auto">
